    },
    {
      "sort": 1500000,
      "name": "Scale Ships",
      "type": "text",
      "_id": "0ktyrDh0gNgr1qgw",
      "system": {},
      "title": {
        "show": true,
        "level": 1
      },
      "image": {},
      "text": {
        "format": 1,
        "content": "<p>Automatically scales spacecraft tokens. Spaeccraft are big, and their sizes vary considerably from a 10t launch or fighter up to a 250,000t dreadnaught. Spacecraft are also small relative to the grid scale.</p><p>This macro will apply a logorithmic scaling to tokens based on their tonnage. This does not take the scene grid into account. It scales tokens to fit a number of grid squares, regardless of how large that grid is.</p><p>There are four options, based on how large the tokens you want to focus on are:</p><ul><li><p>Smallcraft - for when most ships are fighters or smallcraft. Spacecraft over 100t will appear as very large. A Far Trader token will be 4x4 grid units in size.</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Spacecraft - for when most ships are in the 100t to 1,000t range. Small fighters will appear as sub-grid sized tokens. A Far Trader is 3x3 grid units in size.</p></li><li><p>Large Ships - for when ships are 1,000t or larger. A Far Trader is 1x1 grid units in size.</p></li><li><p>Capital Ships - for when the main ships are massive capital ships. A Far Trader token will appear as a quarter of a grid.</p></li></ul><p>@UUID[Compendium.mgt2e.base-macros.Macro.BAV1Tj8rE0i9eTsT]{Scale Ships}</p>"
      },
      "video": {
        "controls": true,
        "volume": 0.5
      },
      "src": null,
      "category": null,
      "ownership": {
        "default": -1,
        "mhUjqDVicnwIUaiq": 3
      },
      "flags": {},
      "_stats": {
        "compendiumSource": null,
        "duplicateSource": null,
        "exportSource": null,
        "coreVersion": "13.351",
        "systemId": "mgt2e",
        "systemVersion": "0.23.3.4-DEV",
        "createdTime": 1792854088118,
        "modifiedTime": 1792854649311,
        "lastModifiedBy": "mhUjqDVicnwIUaiq"
      },
      "_key": "!journal.pages!f61FiaIEjs2FbDRw.0ktyrDh0gNgr1qgw"
    },
    {
      "sort": 1600000,
      "name": "Scale Worlds",
      "type": "text",
      "_id": "Cz4OC0yQ0R3XY2ny",
      "system": {},
      "title": {
        "show": true,
        "level": 1
      },
      "image": {},
      "text": {
        "format": 1,
        "content": "<p>This scales world tokens. If a token represents a World, then it will be scaled according to the actual size of the world. This can be used in spacecraft combat scenes, where ships are in orbit and you want a world as 'terrain' that matches the grid size.</p><p>Note that this assumes a sensible grid size. If the grid unit is not \"km\", or the grid scale is less than 100km, then the macro will not run.</p><p>Assuming these requirements are met, then the world token will be scaled according to the world size defined in the UWP.</p><p>@UUID[Compendium.mgt2e.base-macros.Macro.qaDapPxzkNdklekX]{Scale Worlds}</p>"
      },
      "video": {
        "controls": true,
        "volume": 0.5
      },
      "src": null,
      "category": null,
      "ownership": {
        "default": -1,
        "mhUjqDVicnwIUaiq": 3
      },
      "flags": {},
      "_stats": {
        "compendiumSource": null,
        "duplicateSource": null,
        "exportSource": null,
        "coreVersion": "13.351",
